3682: \begin{proposition}[Venue-submission pack gate]
3683: \label{audit:venue-submission-pack-gate}
3684: Assume that, at final upload time, the CICM presentation-only call still has the
3685: venue rules listed in Table~\ref{tab:venue-submission-pack-gate}, as certified by
3686: the fresh finite record required in
3687: Theorem~\ref{thm:venue-rule-freshness-non-escalation}.  Then the
3688: current package is submission-pack ready for this route exactly when the finite
3689: gate in that table passes: the primary artifact is the two-page-plus-bibliography
3690: source \path{submission_abstract.tex}, the LNCS-style source and bibliography
3691: files are present, the selected exact support surface
3692: \path{review_bundle/} is supplied with
3693: \path{review_bundle/FINAL_DIGESTS_SHA256.md} and the root
3694: \path{theorem_inventory.json} coordinate named there, and the title/author
3695: metadata remains in the primary source.  This gate is a local readiness
3696: certificate only; it does not assert EasyChair upload, reviewer approval,
3697: acceptance, camera-ready approval, or proceedings publication.
3698: \end{proposition}
3699: 
3700: 
3701: \medskip
3702: \begin{proof}
3703: The table has five rows, so the check is finite.  The route-class row compares
3704: the venue's presentation-only rule with the local role separation already fixed
3705: by Proposition~\ref{prop:final-package-shape-convention}:
3706: \path{submission_abstract.tex} is primary, while \path{main.tex},
3707: \path{theorem_inventory.json}, and exact \path{review_bundle/} inclusion are
3708: support artifacts.  If the primary artifact is not the short source, if those
3709: support artifacts are presented as a second primary proceedings paper, or if the
3710: bundle branch is silently changed to an unrecorded archive replacement, this row
3711: fails.  If it passes, the row proves only compatibility with the
3712: presentation-only artifact split, because its
3713: boundary column expressly excludes acceptance and proceedings-publication
3714: claims.
3715: 
3716: The formatting row is a syntactic source check.  The manuscript begins with the
3717: LNCS class \path{llncs}; the package uses \path{splncs04} for the bibliography;
3718: and the local compiled short artifact and bibliography files are present as
3719: \path{submission_abstract.pdf} and \path{submission_abstract.bbl}.  These are
3720: finite path and token checks.  They do not inspect Springer production systems,
3721: nor do they prove that the venue will accept the formatting; hence the row gives
3722: local formatting readiness only.  The supplement-access row is finite because it
3723: requires the selected exact bundle files, the final digest manifest, and the
3724: root theorem-inventory coordinate named by the manifest and certificate ledger.
3725: Audit record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} remains only the
3726: criterion that would have to be satisfied by a future archive replacement; it is
3727: not the branch selected by the current source package.  The metadata and
3728: bibliography row checks the title, author block, institute/email block,
3729: bibliography command, and \path{references.bib}; it does not certify external
3730: metadata entry.  The deadline row records only that the package can be checked
3731: against the venue date before upload and does not assert that an upload was made.
3732: 
3733: If all rows pass, each venue-facing submission claim used by this manuscript has
3734: a finite witness and an explicit negative boundary, so the package is ready in
3735: the limited local sense stated in the proposition.  Conversely, if any row fails,
3736: one of the finite route-class, formatting, supplement-access, metadata,
3737: bibliography, or deadline witnesses required by the table is absent or stale;
3738: there is then no local certificate for submission-pack readiness.  The final
3739: sentence follows from the boundary column and from
3740: Definition~\ref{def:operational-acceptance-interface}: external upload,
3741: acceptance, camera-ready approval, and publication are editorial or venue events,
3742: not local finite-record consequences of this gate.\end{proof}
3743: 
3744: \begin{proposition}[Submission artifact role separation]
3745: \label{audit:submission-artifact-role-separation}
3746: For the current presentation-only route, the primary artifact, long technical
3747: supplement, and review bundle have distinct review roles.  The primary source
3748: \path{submission_abstract.tex} states the presentation claim, \path{main.tex}
3749: proves the long-form interface theorems and records the case tables, and
3750: \path{review_bundle/} supplies the supplemental source snapshots, case snapshots,
3751: and machine-readable manifest rows.  None of these roles converts the support
3752: bundle into a second primary submission or converts a primary-artifact claim into
3753: an uncited supplement claim.
3754: \end{proposition}
3755: 
3756: 
3757: \medskip
3758: \begin{proof}
3759: The manifest field \path{submission_artifacts} names the short source, intended
3760: short PDF, long technical source, long technical PDF, and supplemental bundle as
3761: separate artifacts.  The checklist above fixes how the short artifact points to
3762: the supplement: it names the safety theorem, the case rows, the evidence-level
3763: boundary, and \path{review_bundle/}.  The earlier source-snapshot and
3764: case-snapshot propositions identify the two support functions of the bundle: a
3765: pinned discovery-gate source snapshot and bounded case-evidence snapshots.  Since
3766: the primary note states only the interface and each support claim is tied to a
3767: specific theorem, table, or manifest field, the artifacts remain role-separated:
3768: the support materials make the primary note reviewable but do not become hidden
3769: primary claims.\end{proof}
