4202: \begin{proposition}[Primary-claim conditional inventory-audit classification]
4203: \label{prop:primary-claim-row-classification}
4204: Assume the current primary source \path{submission_abstract.tex} is the submitted
4205: primary artifact, the twelve-row inventory
4206: \path{review_bundle/primary_claim_inventory.json} is supplied with the review
4207: bundle or an accepted archive-equivalent support surface, and the finite manual
4208: inventory audit has identified \path{pc1},\ldots,\path{pc12} as the load-bearing
4209: primary assertions.  Then the current primary-claim inventory is complete for
4210: the short presentation note in the following conditional inventory-audit sense.
4211: Rows \path{pc1}, \path{pc8}, \path{pc9}, \path{pc10}, \path{pc11}, and
4212: \path{pc12} are accepted certificate rows at the evidence level named in
4213: Table~\ref{tab:primary-claim-inventory}.  Rows \path{pc2}, \path{pc3},
4214: \path{pc4}, \path{pc5}, and \path{pc7} are bounded contextual interface rows.
4215: Row \path{pc6} is accepted only through the bounded artifact certificate $a_6$.
4216: Relative to that finite audit, there is no remaining non-classified or hidden
4217: load-bearing primary assertion.
4218: \end{proposition}
4219: 
4220: \begin{proof}
